@{
    var resourcePath = "~/Views/MemberRequests/Guidelines/th-th/Agent/Styles/";
}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=0.7, user-scalable=yes">
    <title>Play For Fun</title>
    <link href='https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Roboto' rel='stylesheet' type='text/css'>
    <link type="text/css" rel="stylesheet" href="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/page.css")" />
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="feature-desc">
            <span><span class="bold">'Play for Fun'</span> on member site allows members to trial new products with virtual currency before requesting a product activation for the real play. To support user in managing these requests, the new feature with the same name has been created to provide you the number of pending requests and the quick way to enable them.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-images">
            <figure>
                <img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/f1.png")" alt="Fig 1">
                <figcaption>Figure 1. 'Play for Fun' Dashboard</figcaption>
            </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-list">
            <div class="feature">
                <div class="feature-title">1. Product Activation</div>

                <div class="feature-desc">Follow these step-by-step directions and learn how to enable a product for your member.</div>

                <div class="step-level">
                    <div class="feature-desc">
                        <span><span class="bold">Step 1.</span> Open member request list via one of two ways below:</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="alphabet-ordered">
                        <p>a. In Home page, click on the request number.</p>
                        <div class="feature-images">
                            <figure>
                                <img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/f2.png")" alt="Fig 2">
                                <figcaption>Figure 2. Play for Fun in Home page</figcaption>
                            </figure>
                        </div>

                        <p>b. In Member Information menu, click on <span class="bold">Play For Fun – Member Request.</span></p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="step-level">
                    <div class="feature-desc">
                        <span class="bold">Step 2.</span> Select the account that you wish to enable and configure the settings.
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-images">
                        <figure>
                            <img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/f3.png")" alt="Fig 3">
                            <figcaption>Figure 3. Play for Fun - Member Request</figcaption>
                        </figure>
                    </div>

                    <ul class="level-1">
                        <li>
                            <span class="bold">Action</span> Click to open setting page.
                            <ul class="level-2">
                                <li>
                                    <span class="icon"><img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/sync.png")" alt="Icon Sync"></span>Sync: Account has not been synced with Casino.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <span class="icon"><img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/pencil.png")" alt="Icon Edit"> </span>Edit: Account has already been synced Casino.
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            Member balance information in real currency:
                            <ul class="level-2">
                                <li><span class="bold">Balance</span>: Total win/loss amount of member including today win/loss.</li>
                                <li><span class="bold">Outstanding</span>:  Total betting amount on running tickets.</li>
                                <li><span class="bold">Bet Credit</span>: Total available amount of member, which can be used to place bet.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            Please contact upline if:
                            <ul class="level-2">
                                <li>You cannot enable product, which has not been enabled by upline yet.</li>

                                <div class="feature-images">
                                    <figure>
                                        <img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/f4.png")" alt="Fig 4">
                                        <figcaption>Figure 4. Upline has not enabled this product for your account</figcaption>
                                    </figure>
                                </div>

                                <li>You are able to enable product, but cannot configure settings.</li>

                                <div class="feature-images">
                                    <figure>
                                        <img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/f5.png")" alt="Fig 4">
                                        <figcaption>Figure 5. Upline has not configured product’s settings for your account</figcaption>
                                    </figure>
                                </div>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="step-level">
                    <div class="feature-desc">
                        <span class="bold">Step 3.</span> Click on the icon
                        <span class="icon"><img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/sync.png")" alt="Icon Sync"></span> or
                        <span class="icon"><img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/pencil.png")" alt="Icon Edit"> </span>
                        to open Setting page, and then select ‘Enable Casino’ checkbox to enable Casino for selected member.
                        Note that you should configure your own settings before enabling the product.
                    </div>

                    <div class="feature-images">
                        <figure>
                            <img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/f6.png")" alt="Fig 6">
                            <figcaption>Figure 6. Setting page</figcaption>
                        </figure>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="step-level">
                    <span class="bold">Step 4.</span> Click <span class="bold">Submit</span> button to complete product activation.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                <div class="feature-title">2. Member Play For Fun Detail Report</div>

                <div class="feature-desc">
                    Click on product name of the request (or on <span class="bold">Play For Fun Detail</span> in Reports menu) to view statistics of members who have tried the products of Play for Fun.
                </div>

                <div class="feature-images">
                    <figure>
                        <img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/f7.png")" alt="Fig 7">
                        <figcaption>Figure 7. Play For Fun in Home page</figcaption>
                    </figure>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-desc">A Play for Fun report will be opened as below.</div>

                <div class="feature-images">
                    <figure>
                        <img src="@Url.Content(resourcePath+"/Images/f8.png")" alt="Fig 8">
                        <figcaption>Figure 8. Member Play For Fun Detail report</figcaption>
                    </figure>
                </div>

                <div class="feature-desc">
                    Note that the report summarizes members’ statistics on selected product based on virtual currency only.
                    <ul class="level-1">
                        <li>
                            <span class="bold">Status</span>: Product status on member.
                            <ul class="level-2">
                                <li><span class="bold">Enabled</span>: Account has been enabled for selected product.</li>
                                <li><span class="bold">Disabled</span>: Account has not been enabled for selected product.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li><span class="bold">Turnover</span>: Total member stake amount.</li>
                        <li><span class="bold">Member Win Loss</span>: Total member win loss amount.</li>
                        <li><span class="bold">Play count</span>: Total number of bet tickets.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>